{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"viceregal-granite-sloth","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Parent-drift breadcrumb comment (echo-safe, nearest-represented-ancestor)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nWhen a parent relationship can't be represented in Jira (the parent type collapsed to a\nsame/lower hierarchy level, or Jira forbids the parentage), the reconciler already drifts\nvia `pass_io.record_parent_divergence` (alerts `outbound-parent-unrepresentable` /\n`-rejected`). But a dropped parent turns an understandable child into an under-defined\nleaf in Jira: the user sees no hint where the critical parent context lives. Alt-link\nself-heal was rejected (echo-unsafe). We need an echo-safe breadcrumb that points the Jira\nuser at the parent without risking a reconcile echo loop.\n\n## Approach\n\nOn a parent drift, append **once** an echo-safe managed comment naming the **nearest\nrepresented ancestor's Jira key** (not the rebar id — the Jira key is stable and\nuser-navigable). Build it on the existing managed-comment machinery in\n`outbound_comments.py`: carry the `RECONCILER_MARKER` (`<!-- rebar:reconciler-echo -->`)\nso `_is_machine_marker_comment` recognizes it and inbound never echoes it back as user\ncontent; dedupe on body so it appends exactly once (idempotent across passes). Walk\nancestors upward to the nearest one that has a bound Jira key; if an intervening ancestor\nis **skip-synced**, the comment must say so, so the child's situation is described\naccurately regardless of which ancestor is the nearest represented one. If no ancestor has\na bound Jira key, omit the comment entirely (nothing to point at).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/pass_io.py` — emit the breadcrumb on parent\n  divergence (extends `record_parent_divergence`).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_comments.py` — breadcrumb body builder +\n  marker + dedupe (reuses `RECONCILER_MARKER`, `_is_machine_marker_comment`,\n  `_diff_comments`).\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_parent_breadcrumb.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Breadcrumb emitted (unit):** a parent drift with a bound-key parent appends one\n  comment carrying the parent's Jira key and the `RECONCILER_MARKER` — asserted on the\n  comment body + marker.\n- **Idempotent (append-once):** a second pass does not append a duplicate — asserted on\n  the comment count via the body-dedup path.\n- **Skip-synced ancestor noted:** when the nearest represented ancestor sits above a\n  skip-synced intervening ancestor, the body states the skip — asserted on the body text.\n- **Omitted when unbound (failure path):** no ancestor has a bound Jira key ⇒ no comment —\n  asserted on the empty comment set.\n- **Echo-safe:** the breadcrumb is recognized by `_is_machine_marker_comment` and is not\n  re-ingested as user content inbound — asserted on the inbound classification.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A parent drift appends exactly one echo-safe breadcrumb naming the nearest\n  represented ancestor's Jira key — verified by\n  `test_parent_breadcrumb.py::test_breadcrumb_emitted`.\n- [ ] The breadcrumb is append-once/idempotent across passes — verified by\n  `test_parent_breadcrumb.py::test_breadcrumb_idempotent`.\n- [ ] A skip-synced intervening ancestor is noted in the breadcrumb body — verified by\n  `test_parent_breadcrumb.py::test_skip_synced_ancestor_noted`.\n- [ ] No bound-key ancestor ⇒ no breadcrumb — verified by\n  `test_parent_breadcrumb.py::test_breadcrumb_omitted_when_unbound`.\n- [ ] The breadcrumb is marker-tagged and not echoed inbound — verified by\n  `test_parent_breadcrumb.py::test_breadcrumb_echo_safe`.\n\nTest tier: **in-process unit** — breadcrumb body assembly, dedupe, ancestor walk, and the\nmarker classification are pure functions; oracles are the produced comment set/body and the\ninbound machine-marker classification.","id":"2c66-205d-92e1-4419","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Parent-drift breadcrumb comment (echo-safe, nearest-represented-ancestor)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787290330607276001,"uuid":"e0282e85-38be-4adf-97cd-4476fa8a927f"}